E0204: `purity:` is not a key Ply knows. The keys a component accepts are: `anchor`, `checks`, `components`, `fns`, `owns`, `profile`, `pure`, `strict`, `uses`. Did you mean `pure`? A key Ply does not know is almost always a typo, and a typo has to be caught rather than ignored (§5.1a rule 1) -- an ignored key is a contract you think you wrote and Ply never read. Found at `components.pricing.purity` in ply.yaml.
